  vendorName: Glazier Orson
  offerText: Your windowpanes have severe micro-fractures. Pay my premium replacement
    fee now, or they will shatter inward under the slightest atmospheric pressure.
  acceptResultText: You pay for the reinforced glass. It looks exactly the same,
    but you feel completely safe from the unpredictable weather outside.
  rejectResultText: You laugh at his obvious scam. Your windows look perfectly fine,
    and saving your money makes you feel brilliant.
  acceptedDelayedText: 
  rejectedDelayedText: Orson was lying. Your house is fine after the storm. You are
    glad that you didn't get scammed.
